entry.summary:
Hard-coded secrets are the most dangerous vulnerability. They're committed to version control, leaked in logs, exposed in error messages, and stolen in supply chain attacks. Proper secrets management means treating credentials as infrastructure, not code.
Environment variables are the bare minimum, but they're not foolproof.
// Vulnerable
const apiKey = 'sk_live_abc123xyz789';
const db = postgres(`postgresql://${apiKey}@host`);

// Better
const apiKey = process.env.API_KEY;
const db = postgres(`postgresql://${process.env.DB_USER}:${process.env.DB_PASSWORD}@${process.env.DB_HOST}`);

// Validate on startup
if (!process.env.API_KEY) {
  throw new Error('API_KEY environment variable is required');
}

.env Files


Use .gitignore to exclude environment files, and provide .env.example templates.…

Steps: Night Theme Switcher - https://nightthemeswitcher.romainvigier.fr/ or https://extensions.gnome.org/extension/2236/night-theme-switcher/ day.sh with this code to change the theme: gsettings set org.gnome.desktop.interface gtk-theme 'Adwaita-lgiht';
night.sh: gsettings set org.gnome.desktop.interface gtk-theme 'Adwaita-dark';
For sunrise: bash /path/day.sh bash /path/night.sh
Done.
